WEBVTT

00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:06.240
The festival of dreams
to crown the strongest Pokémon Trainer...

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:10.870
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:14.080
The eight mighty trainers
aiming for the summit...

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.080
...have begun battling.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.130
The first match of the semifinals
was Dande versus Carne.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.170
One more Kyodai Hellfire!

00:00:24.170 --> 00:00:25.380
Blow them away!

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.270
Dande emerged victorious.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:42.810
And the second match will be
the Champion of Sinnoh, Shirona, against...

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:45.900
...the first Champion of Alola,
Satoshi.

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.050
All right!

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:16.140
It’s finally time.
I’m counting on you all!

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.520
Satoshi...

00:01:19.310 --> 00:01:20.270
You better win!

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:21.230
Course!

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.400
Now, let’s move!

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.870
I’m cheering for you.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:35.740
Thank you.

00:01:35.740 --> 00:01:37.990
I’ll show you
that I’m worthy of your hope.

00:01:38.370 --> 00:01:42.420
You’re the one
who’ll end Dande’s win streak.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.170
That’s a lot of pressure.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.630
I’ve decided something.

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:48.880
What is it?

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:51.130
Once this tournament’s over...

00:01:51.130 --> 00:01:53.180
I’m retiring from battles.

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:54.340
Huh?!

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:57.470
Ms. Shirona...

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.950
Very well! Everyone is here!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:44.830
Well then,
let’s cheer for Satoshi!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:51.840
The Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament!

00:03:53.630 --> 00:04:00.640
This tournament has truly been a special one,
with Champions gathered from various regions!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:03.100
It’s the second match
of the semifinals!

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:08.640
Ranked 8th in the Masters Eight,
Competitor Satoshi steps onto the field.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:14.320
Bearing the monumental title of
first-ever Champion of Alola,

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:17.530
he has boldly climbed
all the way to the semifinals.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.910
What sort of battle
will he show us today?

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:33.170
Next, ranked 2nd in the Masters Eight,
Competitor Shirona steps onto the field.

00:04:34.420 --> 00:04:37.170
As everyone knows,
she is the Champion of Sinnoh!

00:04:37.170 --> 00:04:41.930
She has the strength and
imposing presence of a queen!

00:04:44.470 --> 00:04:48.020
Now, who will be the one
to battle Competitor Dande?

00:04:48.020 --> 00:04:51.560
Competitor Shirona?
Or Competitor Satoshi?

00:04:53.060 --> 00:04:56.030
That’s right!
All eyes are on this battle, meow!

00:04:56.030 --> 00:04:59.820
And we’ll be passionately commentating
their white-hot battle all the way!

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.030
Above all, Competitor Shirona’s Pokémon
are sure to be strong!

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:04.990
You’ve gotta see ‘em!

00:05:07.790 --> 00:05:11.170
The semifinals are 6v6 full battles!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:14.670
There is no limit on match length
or switching out Pokémon.

00:05:14.670 --> 00:05:19.920
Whoever makes all six of their opponent’s Pokémon
unable to battle will be the winner.

00:05:19.920 --> 00:05:26.930
Additionally, per match, you are allowed a single use of only
one of the following: Daimax, a Z-Move, or Mega Evolution.

00:05:26.930 --> 00:05:30.350
In the first round, Competitor Shirona
used Mega Evolution,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.730
and Competitor Satoshi
used a Z-Move.

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:36.070
Will they play the same cards
in the semifinals?

00:05:36.070 --> 00:05:40.110
Now then, both battlers,
send your first Pokémon out onto the field!

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:40.950
Three!

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:42.030
Two!

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:42.860
One!

00:05:42.860 --> 00:05:43.610
Go!

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:45.580
Kairyu, I choose you!

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.830
Tremble, souls! Mikaruge!

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:02.470
Mikaruge!

00:06:02.470 --> 00:06:06.970
What a surprise! Competitor Shirona’s first Pokémon
is the Sealed Pokémon, Mikaruge!

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:09.430
That Pokémon’s
supposed to be strong?

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.560
I’d call it more creepy
than strong, meow.

00:06:11.560 --> 00:06:16.060
No, no! The Champion of Sinnoh
sent out that Pokémon! It <i>has</i> to be strong!

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:20.860
You can’t let your guard down
against her, Satoshi!

00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:26.450
What a play. She took control of the field
by using a Pokémon nobody had predicted.

00:06:26.450 --> 00:06:27.740
Yeah.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.750
My Kairyu’s not gonna lose,
no matter who she’s up against!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.830
Let the battle begin!

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:36.750
Draco Meteor!

00:06:40.130 --> 00:06:40.960
Surprise Attack!

00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:51.720
A Surprise Attack
steals Kairyu’s thunder!

00:07:17.630 --> 00:07:21.130
It’s laughing!
What a display of toughness from Mikaruge!

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.880
Dragon Claw!

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:26.300
Hypnosis!

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:41.570
Kairyu!

00:07:41.570 --> 00:07:44.320
And she falls asleep!

00:07:44.990 --> 00:07:47.660
This isn’t good!
This isn’t good for Kairyu!

00:07:48.280 --> 00:07:50.950
She won’t be waking up
easily from that...

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.700
Dream Eater!

00:08:02.590 --> 00:08:08.220
Dream Eater, a move that
drains a sleeping Pokémon’s stamina, hits its mark!

00:08:11.260 --> 00:08:12.640
What a combo...

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.100
That’s scary...

00:08:14.100 --> 00:08:15.680
Keep using Dream Eater!

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.410
Now that’s evil...

00:08:30.410 --> 00:08:32.120
See? Told you it’s strong!

00:08:32.120 --> 00:08:35.750
Kairyu’s power is being sucked up
little by little, meow...

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:41.750
Kairyu! Wake up!
C’mon, wake up!

00:08:43.210 --> 00:08:45.550
She shows no sign of responding.

00:08:47.210 --> 00:08:48.510
This...

00:08:48.510 --> 00:08:50.430
Kairyu!

00:08:52.720 --> 00:08:54.470
Kairyu is unable to battle!

00:08:56.140 --> 00:08:57.560
No way...

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:02.730
Competitor Satoshi
has already lost his first Pokémon!

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:13.700
His Kairyu barely did anything...

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:16.660
Return, Kairyu!

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:22.120
Sorry.
I won’t make the same mistake again.

00:09:24.040 --> 00:09:25.750
Return, Mikaruge!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:30.510
Oh? Competitor Shirona
recalls her Mikaruge!

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.430
Come out, Gänger!

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.640
Bloom, Roserade!

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:45.650
Now, next up is
Roserade versus Gänger!

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:49.900
Is Satoshi gonna Daimax it
to turn the tide?!

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:51.110
I don’t know...

00:09:52.570 --> 00:09:57.120
This is how the Champion of Sinnoh,
Ms. Shirona, battles...

00:09:58.290 --> 00:09:59.450
Roserade...

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.960
Seed Machine Gun!

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.130
Shadow Ball!

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:15.680
Seed Machine Gun
isn’t very effective on Gänger!

00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:19.600
Yet, Roserade remains confident!

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:20.680
Will-O-Wisp!

00:10:24.190 --> 00:10:25.690
Leaf Storm!

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:42.410
All right!

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.920
Neither managed
to block the attack.

00:10:44.920 --> 00:10:48.880
But Roserade was burned
by the effect of Will-O-Wisp!

00:10:48.880 --> 00:10:50.960
That’ll eat away at its stamina!

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:52.840
Return, Roserade.

00:10:55.890 --> 00:10:58.390
Competitor Shirona
recalls her Pokémon again!

00:10:58.720 --> 00:11:01.600
And here I thought the Will-O-Wisp
would give him the upper hand...

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:04.520
She’s not giving up control,
no matter what...

00:11:05.770 --> 00:11:07.400
Gänger! Let’s keep going!

00:11:09.020 --> 00:11:11.860
One more time, Mikaruge!

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:16.360
Mikaruge returns?!

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.950
Again?!

00:11:18.950 --> 00:11:22.040
We’re not falling for
Hypnosis or Dream Eater again!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:25.250
So it’s a Ghost type showdown!

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:26.500
Magical Shine!

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:27.500
Surprise Attack!

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.260
Magical Shine and Surprise Attack
are both super effective!

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.430
Gänger!

00:11:56.530 --> 00:11:59.370
One more time, Mikaruge!

00:12:02.120 --> 00:12:03.740
Mikaruge returns?!

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:06.540
Again?!

00:12:06.540 --> 00:12:09.920
We’re not falling for
Hypnosis or Dream Eater again!

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.170
Magical Shine!

00:12:11.170 --> 00:12:12.170
Surprise Attack!

00:12:23.890 --> 00:12:25.020
Gänger!

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:29.020
And they’ve now both
taken heavy damage...

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:32.020
Will they be able to
recover from this?!

00:12:50.170 --> 00:12:51.920
Good job, Gänger!

00:12:56.710 --> 00:12:58.550
Gänger is unable to battle!

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.220
Mikaruge gives Competitor Satoshi
another black mark!

00:13:04.220 --> 00:13:08.060
The switch-up
from Roserade paid off!

00:13:10.850 --> 00:13:13.440
This is looking pretty tough
for Satoshi...

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:16.360
Don’t worry.
The battle’s barely started.

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:19.280
Things <i>really</i> aren’t
going his way today...

00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:21.910
That Champion of Sinnoh’s
just too strong, meow...

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:25.280
We can’t get fired up
when the battle’s <i>this</i> one-sided!

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.120
Return, Gänger!

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:34.460
I’m gonna make the most
of all your effort.

00:13:34.460 --> 00:13:36.500
Return, Mikaruge!

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:41.010
Oh! Competitor Shirona
recalls Mikaruge yet again!

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.340
Is she concerned about the damage
from Magical Shine?!

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:46.140
Unfurl your blessed wings,

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:46.970
Togekiss!

00:13:50.730 --> 00:13:52.730
Togekiss?

00:13:53.520 --> 00:13:57.940
Togekiss! Jubilee Pokémon!
Fairy/Flying type!

00:13:57.940 --> 00:14:00.650
Known as a bringer of blessings,

00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:04.320
it’s been depicted on good-luck charms
since ancient times!

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:06.200
Switching again...

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:08.870
She might be doing this
to throw him off his game.

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.330
Don’t panic.

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:15.380
Don’t let Ms. Shirona
set the pace!

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:18.590
Pikachu...!

00:14:18.590 --> 00:14:20.010
Counting on you!

00:14:23.380 --> 00:14:26.260
Competitor Satoshi’s
third Pokémon is Pikachu!

00:14:26.260 --> 00:14:31.020
We can look forward to the 10,000,000 Volts Z-Move
that decided his first round match.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.810
Turning the tide
with his greatest partner...

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.060
That’ll be Satoshi’s plan.

00:14:38.650 --> 00:14:40.650
Sending Pikachu out now, huh?

00:14:40.650 --> 00:14:42.190
It’s up to you, Pikachu!

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:48.950
Let’s do this, Pikachu!

00:14:48.950 --> 00:14:50.450
100,000 Volts!

00:14:52.910 --> 00:14:54.040
Air Slash!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:06.720
It hits!

00:15:06.720 --> 00:15:08.850
Togekiss is tossing
Pikachu around!

00:15:08.850 --> 00:15:09.930
Pikachu!

00:15:13.930 --> 00:15:15.310
Mind Headbutt!

00:15:15.310 --> 00:15:16.150
Electroweb!

00:15:19.980 --> 00:15:21.610
What’s wrong, Pikachu?!

00:15:25.610 --> 00:15:26.160
Pikachu!

00:15:26.160 --> 00:15:29.410
Togekiss’s ability
is Heaven’s Blessings.

00:15:29.410 --> 00:15:30.410
Yeah.

00:15:30.410 --> 00:15:32.790
So its ability helped flinch him...

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:36.170
You’re really using all sorts of tricks,
Champion of Sinnoh!

00:15:36.170 --> 00:15:38.290
Return, Togekiss!

00:15:38.670 --> 00:15:39.420
What?!

00:15:39.960 --> 00:15:41.960
Another recall!

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.920
Pikachu! Are you okay?

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.890
Emerge from the waves!

00:15:49.890 --> 00:15:50.800
Tritodon!

00:15:58.310 --> 00:16:00.770
Electric moves won’t work on Tritodon!

00:16:00.770 --> 00:16:03.280
Ms. Shirona knows Satoshi well.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:08.160
She’s expecting he’ll keep Pikachu in,
and plans to take him out!

00:16:11.580 --> 00:16:13.330
Earth Power!

00:16:19.040 --> 00:16:21.130
Pikachu, jump!

00:16:25.550 --> 00:16:26.510
I thought so.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:28.760
Iron Tail!

00:16:30.010 --> 00:16:31.550
Stone Edge!

00:16:34.890 --> 00:16:36.930
All right! Hit ‘em!

00:16:41.190 --> 00:16:43.270
That’s it! Send ‘em flying!

00:16:49.990 --> 00:16:53.950
But Tritodon just
absorbs the impact!

00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:55.200
Now!

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:56.250
Lightning Speed!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.220
Tritodon is unable to battle!

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:13.720
The first black mark
for Competitor Shirona!

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:15.010
We did it!

00:17:16.520 --> 00:17:19.270
Good work, Satoshi, Pikachu!

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:20.940
This’s a comeback!
A comeback!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:23.480
Marvelous!
That’s our Pikachu!

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.280
Our training wasn’t
all for naught, meow!

00:17:26.280 --> 00:17:29.490
He’s still got that glittery strength!

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:33.070
Huh?

00:17:33.070 --> 00:17:34.700
Is it over?

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:38.500
Type match-ups truly are
nothing to Satoshi.

00:17:38.500 --> 00:17:40.710
His rhythm of attacks
is wonderful, too.

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:43.210
This is my kind of battle!

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:50.090
Now we’re getting to
see Satoshi’s strengths.

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:56.850
His will to find opportunity in a crisis,
and Pikachu’s skill in seizing it... They’re both incredible.

00:17:58.100 --> 00:18:00.930
Pikachu!
Let’s keep this going!

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.810
Return, Tritodon!

00:18:05.190 --> 00:18:07.150
You fought well.

00:18:07.150 --> 00:18:08.440
Leave the rest to me.

00:18:10.440 --> 00:18:11.900
Come out, Mikaruge!

00:18:17.910 --> 00:18:20.620
Mikaruge makes
its third appearance!

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:21.660
There it is...

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.420
Don’t worry, Pikachu.

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:26.670
I have a plan.

00:18:27.130 --> 00:18:29.210
Spin around using 100,000 Volts!

00:18:33.260 --> 00:18:34.180
What is that?!

00:18:34.180 --> 00:18:35.970
It’s like he’s breakdancing!

00:18:45.310 --> 00:18:48.270
It’s too early for a victory dance.

00:18:48.270 --> 00:18:50.030
Hypnosis!

00:18:52.440 --> 00:18:58.580
Wow! Blocked by Pikachu’s 100,000 Volts,
Mikaruge’s Hypnosis can’t reach him!

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.830
That can’t...

00:18:59.830 --> 00:19:00.990
Finish it!

00:19:03.620 --> 00:19:07.420
It’s like they say...
Offense is the best defense!

00:19:10.500 --> 00:19:11.670
Ms. Shirona!

00:19:11.670 --> 00:19:16.390
That was Counter Shield, a move we came up with
when we traveled through Sinnoh!

00:19:17.760 --> 00:19:21.810
I remember it!
You showed it off at the Sinnoh League.

00:19:21.810 --> 00:19:25.020
We’re stronger
than we were back then!

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.900
Pikachu, Electroweb!

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:28.400
Surprise Attack!

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.570
Now! Iron Tail!

00:19:40.030 --> 00:19:41.870
Mikaruge, go ahead!

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:51.630
All right!

00:19:57.300 --> 00:20:00.140
He beat Mikaruge!

00:20:11.820 --> 00:20:13.110
What is this?

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:15.530
What?!

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:25.290
Pikachu!

00:20:25.830 --> 00:20:28.540
It’s Drag Along!

00:20:38.930 --> 00:20:42.300
Mikaruge and Pikachu are both
unable to battle!

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:46.680
An unbelievable double knockout!

00:20:46.680 --> 00:20:52.690
Drag Along is a fearsome move with which
the defeated Pokémon also takes down its opponent.

00:20:54.020 --> 00:20:58.320
Now Competitor Shirona has four Pokémon left.
Competitor Satoshi is left with three Pokémon.

00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:03.330
Having lost Pikachu,
he can’t use his Z-Move, 10,000,000 Volts!

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:06.120
Pikachu was Satoshi’s ace.

00:21:06.120 --> 00:21:08.830
He’s just suffered
immeasurable damage.

00:21:08.830 --> 00:21:13.590
Well, now...
This is getting interesting, eh, Satoshi?

00:21:17.260 --> 00:21:20.380
Mikaruge...
You truly fought well.

00:21:21.760 --> 00:21:23.220
Rest yourself.

00:21:26.140 --> 00:21:28.770
Ms. Shirona’s strong...

00:21:30.890 --> 00:21:33.100
Pikachu is already down.

00:21:33.690 --> 00:21:37.820
Shirona stands tall before Satoshi
and his hopes of reaching the finals.

00:21:38.530 --> 00:21:41.400
Their fierce fight is only just
beginning!

00:23:06.360 --> 00:23:10.870
<i>Pokémon World Championships
Masters Tournament News!</i>

00:23:11.540 --> 00:23:14.290
What a shock!
Competitor Brat Boy’s Pikachu is down!

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.420
And Competitor Shirona
hasn’t even sent out Gaburias yet!

00:23:17.420 --> 00:23:20.460
What’re you gonna do, brat boy?!
You’ve gotta do something! Hey!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.170
Morpeko, gimme that!

00:23:24.800 --> 00:23:26.640
Calm down, Morpeko!

00:23:26.640 --> 00:23:28.510
We’re live, you know?!

00:23:29.100 --> 00:23:30.680
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:23:30.680 --> 00:23:32.430
The Semifinals III - “Valor”

00:23:32.430 --> 00:23:34.350
Let’s all tune in, meow!
